<article class="env-lemma" id="75AB2F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/75AB2F">Lemma <span data-tag="75AB2F">6.1.4.8</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a presentable $\infty $-category and suppose given a diagram $U: \Nerve (\calI )^{op} \rightarrow \calC $, which we may depict as </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { U_{1} \ar @<.5ex>[r] \ar @<-.5ex>[r] &amp;  U_0 \ar [r] &amp;  U_{-1}}  \]
</div>
  <p> Let $V_{\bullet } = i_{!} U \in \calX _{\Delta _{+}}$ be a left Kan extension of $U$ along $i: \Nerve (\calJ )^{op} \rightarrow \cDelta _{+}^{op}$. Then the augmentation maps $V_0 \rightarrow V_{-1}$ and $U_0 \rightarrow U_{-1}$ are equivalent in the $\infty $-category $\calO _{\calX }$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/6B7471" data-tag="6B7471">4.3.3.8</a>, since $\Hom _{\calI }(\Delta ^ i, \bullet ) \simeq \Hom _{\cDelta _{+}}( \Delta ^ i, \bullet )$ for $i \leq 0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>